{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_007: multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/ViT-L/transformer/concat at 50.7% acc), evidence is sparse and the most important uncertainty is whether the complex transformer aggregation over cells is actually contributing or introducing overfitting/noise. Config_009 changes exactly one variable—aggregation from transformer to avgpool—while keeping scgpt, ViT-L, multiprofile, and concat fusion identical to config_007. This clean A/B test will clarify whether the attention-based aggregation is a meaningful driver of the current performance or whether a simpler mean-pooling suffices. If avgpool matches or beats transformer, it frees us to focus budget on RNA/image encoder choices; if it is substantially worse, it confirms transformer aggregation as a key component. This is the highest-information single-variable probe available at experiment 2, reducing uncertainty about a high-impact architectural choice before committing remaining budget to other dimensions."
}

